  "description": "Our Peñalosa model get its namesake from two brothers – Gil and Enrique Peñalosa. Enrique is currently serving his 2nd term as the Mayor of Bogota, Columbia. Although he did not invent the Ciclovia – a day where pedestrians and bicyclists take back the streets from cars, they have done more to champion this day and spread its message around the world. Our Penalosa “Folding bike” model is the most approachable bike in the bunch. It has a super low step through frame due to its 20″ wheels making the bike easy on and off for people of all sizes. Don’t be fooled, this bike has plenty of pep and can keep up with our larger bikes no problem. With the comfortable upright seating position you’ll feel like you’re riding a cruiser bike yet still able to get plenty of power and go uphills effortlessly. Plus, the Penalosa FOLDS. This bike is like a little transformer as it folds down to the size of a piece of luggage and is then perfect for transporting in your car, on your RV or in your tiny home! The Penalosa is the perfect bike for short and tall riders alike as it’s fully adjustable with a ton of power all wrapped up in our smallest package.",
